<title>INDIA: INDIA'S CEAT 1996/97 PROFIT DOWN.</title>
<headline>INDIA'S CEAT 1996/97 PROFIT DOWN.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 30,1997</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Gross profit	    194.2  vs     498.2</p>
<p>    Income		 13,193.5  vs  17,268.1</p>
<p>    Depreciation	    128.1  vs     322.9</p>
<p>    Tax			  10.0  vs	 3.7</p>
<p>    Amt available for     282.7  vs     357.4</p>
<p>appropriation after</p>
<p>adjustment</p>
<p>    Div (rupees)		2.0  vs	 NA</p>
<p>Note: Ceat Ltd is a leading Indian tyre manufacturer. The company said the figures for the previous period were not comparable as they cover a period of 18 months and include the operations of the tyre cord division for seven months of that period.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom (91-22-265 9000)</p>
</text>
